<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bundela</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bundela Rajputs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelas">Bundelas</a> are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> clan of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> who gave their name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>, the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> and the Vindhya hills. Rising to power in the 16th century, they ruled from Orchha, where the Mughal ally Bir Singh Deo built palaces and temples. In the late 17th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrasal">Chhatrasal</a> Bundela founded the kingdom of Panna, and Bundela houses ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> such as Orchha, Datia and Panna until 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bundela.jpg" alt="Bundela" width="232" height="494" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mydust · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandela.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
